From ad5156dedbc6d47221c62ead178e9b69a9830c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:04:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 149/158] hydra + util: textures inside a usdz archive;
 material:binding:full resolved

Every MEGALIB asset is a usdz with its textures inside, so a texture's
resolved path is asset.usdz[textures/color.jpg], which OpenImageIO cannot
open: Cycles painted it magenta where Karma, reading through USD's
resolver, showed it. HdCyclesArchiveImageLoader takes the bytes from
ArGetResolver().OpenAsset and decodes them from memory through an IOProxy
parameter added to ImageMetaData::oiio_load_metadata/pixels; the material
binds it on every image node whose file is in an archive, as it does for
COP textures. The ar library joins the USD libraries linked. (K-111)

Houdini's Assign Material LOP, asked for a purpose, writes
material:binding:full, which the Hydra 2 emulation does not resolve for
this delegate despite GetMaterialBindingPurpose: the prim rendered with the
default surface. A HdsiMaterialBindingResolvingSceneIndex registered for
both renderers copies the first binding found, full then all-purpose, onto
the all-purpose one. (K-112)

The SVM compiler's virtual stack of 0148 is dropped; the report of the live
values at an overflow and the per-shader peak stay. Cycles nodes keep their
Hydra names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
